# Controller RF station power. libCVController.so powers the nordic link
# chip by writing the eeprom driver's temp_gpio129 attribute, but that
# node lives on i2c@89c000 which this kernel tree keeps disabled - the
# write silently fails and the station never leaves reset, so no pair
# scan can ever see a wand.
#
# The same pin is exposed by the picovr SPI driver on spi1.0 as
# picovr_gpio129; stock init only chmod'd it and let the lib drive it on
# demand once the stack attached. Driving it from init is what bricked
# the boot: a sysfs store that stalls on the SPI bus blocks init's
# action queue (init runs writes inline), and a board-level fault there
# panics the kernel - either way the device resets the moment
# sys.boot_completed fires. The MCU rail keeps stock's early timing and
# init only leaves the pin writable; the station itself is powered by
# the shell's link layer when it attaches, after the bus has settled and
# where a hang costs one shell thread instead of the boot.

on boot
    write /sys/kernel/debug/mcu52840/mcu_power 1
    chmod 0666 /sys/bus/spi/devices/spi1.0/picovr_gpio129

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    chmod 0666 /sys/bus/spi/devices/spi1.0/picovr_gpio129
